# Terminal crossing structural boundary trace

Selected revision: ff9c1d7d0ea168b7e14eedc5e44879ee7b84fb04.
Registrations: REGISTRATION-TERMINAL-BOUNDARY-L13-3802.json and
REGISTRATION-TERMINAL-INTERPOLATION-L13-3802.json.

- The shared crossing search skips an interval when its right endpoint is not
  terminal, and otherwise binary-searches the terminal predicate. Its
  documented exactness assumes each meter is linear between supplied points.
- Native structural points include disease curve/events and intervention
  start, stop and profile end. Selected intervention effects are constant
  during their active interval; disease curves interpolate between points.
  Combining sources, however, clamps after each addition to [-1, 2], which
  can introduce internal slope changes not explicitly listed by that native
  structural producer. Opposing slopes can in principle create an interior
  peak, but an admitted disease/intervention combination producing a missed
  terminal crossing has not been established.
- Exact prior same-lens physiology evidence, source identity, native profile
  bounds, ordering, reachable mixed slopes and alias reconciliation still need
  qualification. No runtime failure or new unique finding is claimed.
